Subject: [PATCH] drm/amd/pm/si: Limit GPIO DC mode to mobile GPUs

Diagnostic backport of Timur Kristof's September 23, 2026 upstream fix,
"Check AMD_IS_MOBILITY flag for PPSMC_SYSTEMFLAG_GPIO_DC".

The tested D700 GPUs are desktop devices, but their VBIOS sets HARDWAREDC
and defines a 300/150 MHz battery state. Only enable GPIO DC mode for
mobile GPUs, preserving the remaining power and thermal-control flags.

Original patch:
https://www.mail-archive.com/amd-gfx@lists.freedesktop.org/msg151959.html
Maintainer review:
https://www.mail-archive.com/amd-gfx@lists.freedesktop.org/msg152027.html

---
--- a/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/legacy-dpm/si_dpm.c
+++ b/drivers/gpu/drm/amd/pm/legacy-dpm/si_dpm.c
@@ -5263,7 +5263,8 @@ static int si_init_smc_table(struct amdgpu_device *adev)
 		break;
 	}
 
-	if (adev->pm.dpm.platform_caps & ATOM_PP_PLATFORM_CAP_HARDWAREDC)
+	if ((adev->flags & AMD_IS_MOBILITY) &&
+	    (adev->pm.dpm.platform_caps & ATOM_PP_PLATFORM_CAP_HARDWAREDC))
 		table->systemFlags |= PPSMC_SYSTEMFLAG_GPIO_DC;
 
 	if (adev->pm.dpm.platform_caps & ATOM_PP_PLATFORM_CAP_REGULATOR_HOT) {
